ted to the history of Tasmania's association with the sea, ships, and ship-building, and is located in Sullivans Cove, Hobart, Tasmania. Established in 1974, the museum has been based in the former Carnegie Library since 2000.","wpu":"Maritime Museum Tasmania","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Maritime_Museum_of_Tasmania_%282023%29.jpg/960px-Maritime_Museum_of_Tasmania_%282023%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-42.881992,"lo":147.332009,"d":138,"h":"Dec 26-Mar 01 Mo-Su,PH 10:00-16:00; Mar 02-Dec 24 Tu-Su 10:00-16:00; PH Mo 10:00-16:00; Dec 25 off; Apr 25 off; easter -2 days off","w":"https://www.tmag.tas.gov.au/","wp":"en:Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery","ds":"The Tasmanian Museum & Art Gallery (TMAG) is a museum located in Hobart, Tasmania, Australia. The museum was established in 1846, by the Royal Society of Tasmania, the oldest Royal Society outside England. The TMAG receives 400,000 visitors annually.","wpu":"Tasmanian Museum & Art Gallery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/62/Tasmanian_Museum_and_Art_Gallery_logo.svg/960px-Tasmanian_Museum_and_Art_Gallery_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Above and Beyond - Tasmanian Seaplanes","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-42.882847,"lo":147.335266,"d":185,"w":"https://aboveandbeyond.flights/"},{"n":"Self portrait, Louis and Joe","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":-42.882238,"lo":147.335061,"d":188},{"n":"Mantra on Collins","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":-42.880922,"lo":147.33069,"d":297,"wifi":1},{"n":"Mantra on Collins Hobart","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":-42.880871,"lo":147.330682,"d":302,"w":"https://all.accor.com/","wifi":1},{"n":"IXL Apartments","g":"sights","k":"apartment","la":-42.880823,"lo":147.335428,"d":312,"wifi":1},{"n":"Mövenpick Hotel Hobart","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":-42.882605,"lo":14