als","k":"atm","la":-42.883179,"lo":147.326486,"d":531,"w":"https://www.anz.com.au/"},{"n":"Westpac","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":-42.882777,"lo":147.326376,"d":540,"w":"https://www.westpac.com.au/"},{"n":"Commonwealth Bank","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":-42.883243,"lo":147.326335,"d":543,"w":"https://www.commbank.com.au/"},{"n":"Constitution Dock","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.8825,"lo":147.333056,"d":55,"ds":"Constitution Dock is the harbour-side dock area of Hobart, the capital city of the Australian state of Tasmania, in the Port of Hobart, on the River Derwent. The dock is adjacent to other Hobart landmark areas, Victoria Dock, Salamanca Place and Battery Point, and forms part of the foreshore of Sullivans Cove. The dock consists of a rock-walled marina with an opening for boats.","wpu":"Constitution Dock","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Hobart_Wharfchancellor.jpg/960px-Hobart_Wharfchancellor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ingle Hall","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.88203,"lo":147.33076,"d":211,"ds":"Ingle Hall is a landmark building in Hobart, Tasmania on the corner of Macquarie and Argyle Streets. It has served numerous purposes over its history and is vacant; it was most recently used as The Mercury print museum. It is unknown when the building was built as it predates any government record holding by the state of Tasmania, which began in 1822.","wpu":"Ingle Hall","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Hobart_architecture.jpg/960px-Hobart_architecture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Franklin Square (Hobart)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.88334,"lo":147.330248,"d":227,"ds":"Franklin Square is a 1.6-acre (0.63-hectare) oak-lined public square located in the Hobart central business district in Tasmania, Australia. It is named for the British Royal Navy officer and Arctic explorer Sir John Franklin, who served as the 4th Lieutenant-Governor of Van Diemen's Land. The centrepiece of the park is a statue of Franklin, with an epitaph written by Alfred, Lord Tennyson.","wpu":"Franklin Square (Hobart)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Lascar_Franklin_Square_%28Hobart%29_%284552530076%29.jpg/960px-Lascar_Franklin_Square_%28Hobart%29_%284552530076%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St David's Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.886,"lo":147.329,"d":466,"ds":"St David's Park is a heritage-listed park in Hobart, Tasmania, bounded by Davey Street, Salamanca Place, and Sandy Bay Road. The site originally served as Hobart’s primary burial ground and is the final resting place of several early settlers, including its founding Lieutenant Governor, David Collins.","wpu":"St David's Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Hobart_Historical_St_David%27s_Park_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Hobart_Historical_St_David%27s_Park_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hobart Cenotaph","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.8775,"lo":147.336111,"d":662,"ds":"Hobart Cenotaph (usually The Cenotaph, also referred to as Hobart War Memorial) is the main commemorative military monument for the Australian state of Tasmania. It is located in the capital Hobart in a prominent position on the Queens Domain, on a small rise overlooking the city and River Derwent. The Cenotaph sits directly above what was once the location of the Queens Battery.","wpu":"Hobart Cenotaph","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Hobart-War-Memorial-Cenotaph-2008.jpg/960px-Hobart-War-Memorial-Cenotaph-2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"State Library of Tasmania","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.881735,"lo":147.324552,"d":702,"ds":"The State Library of Tasmania is the reference, special collections, research and public lending library in the Tasmanian capital of Hobart, Australia. It is part of Libraries Tasmania. Libraries Tasmania includes a state-wide network of library services, community learning, adult literacy and the State’s archives and heritage services.","wpu":"State Library of Tasmania","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/State_Library_of_Tasmania.jpg/960px-State_Library_of_Tasmania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Avalon Theatre, Hobart","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.880572,"lo":147.324436,"d":748,"ds":"The Avalon Theatre is a historic former Temperance Hall, theatre and cinema in Hobart, Tasmania, Australia.","wpu":"Avalon Theatre, Hobart","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Former_Avalon_Theatre_Hobart_Tasmania_Australia.jpg/960px-Former_Avalon_Theatre_Hobart_Tasmania_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Army Museum of Tasmania","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-42.888744,"lo":147.325497,"d":884,"ds":"The Army Museum of Tasmania (formerly known as the Military Museum of Tasmania) is located within Anglesea Barracks in Hobart, Tasmania, Australia. Anglesea Barracks, constructed in 1814. The Barracks is included on the Commonwealth Heritage List.","wpu":"Army Museum of Tasmania","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Military_Museum_of_Tasmania_2010.JPG/960px-Military_Museum_of_Tasmania_2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Hobart ( HOH-bart; Southeast Tasmanian: nipaluna) is the capital and most populous city of the island state of Tasmania, Australia. Located in Tasmania's south-east on the estuary of the River Derwent, it is the southernmost capital city in Australia. Despite containing nearly half of Tasmania's population, Hobart is the least-populated Australian state capital city, and second-smallest by population and area after Darwin(55.859) if territories are taken into account.","wpu":"Hobart","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Franklin_Wharf_2015_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Franklin_Wharf_2015_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}